<title>UK: INSIGHT - Copper expected lower, eyes $2,350.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT - Copper expected lower, eyes $2,350.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> 3 MONTH     CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 * MA10 * MA30</p>
<p> COPPER     2410/15 *  2400   *  2500  *  36   * 2559 * 2513</p>
<p> ALUMINIUM  1562/66 *  1560   *  1590  *  40   * 1591 * 1616</p>
<p>---------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - June 25-----------------</p>
<p>Copper, reeling from recent bouts of liquidation, looks set to tumble to $2,350 a tonne if prices breach $2,400, traders and analysts said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Despite continued falls in LME stocks, aluminium was likely to follow copper lower and might test levels towards $1,550 if support at $1,560/65 gave way, they added.</p>
